From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: glink: TB321FU C1 orientation from TLMM 29

The TB321FU firmware sends an altmode notification, and so an orientation
and a mux state, only for DisplayPort partners. A USB-only partner on the
long-side port (a phone, a drive) left the PS5169 redriver and the QMP PHY
parked and every such device ran at USB 2.0.

TLMM 29 follows the plug orientation on that port (measured: high with
the plug reversed, low with it normal, matching the redriver state the
firmware sets for a DP hub), like the orientation-gpios line of the SM8650
reference boards. Use it as the C1 orientation line, sharing the
descriptor already taken as the secondary audio detect line.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c	2026-11-07 08:47:42.491155025 +0100
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c	2026-11-07 08:47:42.491267684 +0100
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 #include <linux/auxiliary_bus.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
 #include <linux/of_device.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
@@ -629,6 +630,17 @@
 		ucsi->port_orientation[port] = desc;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * TB321FU: TLMM 29, read above as the secondary audio detect line,
+	 * follows the plug orientation on the long-side port (C1), like the
+	 * orientation line of the SM8650 reference boards. Without it a
+	 * USB-only partner gets no orientation and the SuperSpeed lanes stay
+	 * parked, since the firmware only reports one for DisplayPort.
+	 */
+	if (!ucsi->port_orientation[0] && ucsi->secondary_audio_detect &&
+	    of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,tb321fu"))
+		ucsi->port_orientation[0] = ucsi->secondary_audio_detect;
+
 	ucsi->client = devm_pmic_glink_client_alloc(dev, PMIC_GLINK_OWNER_USBC,
 						    pmic_glink_ucsi_callback,
 						    pmic_glink_ucsi_pdr_notify,
